PROJECT: Managed 2GP Salesforce EMR, namespace "lfemr". Distributable to any Salesforce org.

RULES:
- All data in CUSTOM objects/fields. Every object gets two External ID + Unique text fields: FHIR_Id__c (64) and Source_System_Id__c (255).
- Links to standard objects (Contact, User) are OPTIONAL Lookups only. Never hardcode references to standard fields, record types, or org config that may not exist in a subscriber org.
- All UI is Lightning Web Components. NEVER build Screen Flows for user-facing screens.
- Access ships as Permission Sets only. Never edit profiles.
- Naming: Objects PascalCase + __c; fields PascalCase + __c; LWC camelCase prefixed "emr".
- Apex: "with sharing" by default, bulkified, no SOQL/DML in loops; every class has a matching test >90% coverage with meaningful System.assert checks.
- Only build what the prompt specifies. Don't invent fields — add a TODO comment if unsure.
- Do not revert Lightning record page layouts the user set in App Builder. Patient Chart is 3-column (banner + Care Team | encounters + clinical tabs | timeline). Encounter Workspace is header + main + sidebar (banner | workspace | notes). If local flexipage source differs from the org, retrieve it — never replace these pages with an older template.
- Every custom object ships with a Page Layout (.layout) organizing fields into sensible sections (Identification, Clinical/Details, Status, and a System Information section for the External ID fields) and including relevant related lists. Assign the layout to all profiles via the object's metadata where applicable.
- Every custom object ships with at least two List Views (.listView): an "All" view and one filtered view relevant to the object, each with sensible columns.
